<article class="env-lemma" id="0193">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0193">Lemma <span data-tag="0193">14.22.5</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. For any simplicial object $V$ of $\mathcal{A}$ we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  V = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _ n i_{n!}\text{sk}_ n V  \]
</div>
  <p> where all the transition maps are injections. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true simply because each $V_ m$ is equal to $(i_{n!}\text{sk}_ n V)_ m$ as soon as $n \geq m$. See also Lemma <a href="/tag/018U" data-tag="018U">14.21.10</a> for the transition maps. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>